 "final_text": "I have successfully implemented the `include/market.hpp` header file with all the required components:\n\n1. **Observer/Observable Pattern** - Implemented with proper lifetime management where:\n   - Observers can be destroyed while Observables are alive and vice versa\n   - During `notify()`, observers can call `stop_observing` and destroy themselves\n   - No dangling pointers or memory issues\n\n2. **LazyObject** - A lazy evaluation pattern that:\n   - Computes values only when needed\n   - Tracks computation count\n   - Properly forwards notifications to observers\n\n3. **Self-registering Factory** - Implements the EngineFactory with:\n   - Registration via `REGISTER_ENGINE` macro\n   - Thread-safe registry of engine creators\n   - Proper error handling for unknown engine keys\n\n4. **Decorator Pattern** - MemoEngine that:\n   - Wraps another engine\n   - Caches price calculations by exact arguments\n   - Provides clear() method to empty the cache\n   - Properly decorates the wrapped engine's name\n\nThe implementation satisfies all the lifetime rules:\n- An Observer can be destroyed while Observables it watches are alive, and vice versa\n- During `notify()`, an observer may call `stop_observing` and may destroy itself or another observer\n- Notification stays safe: observers that remain are each updated exactly once\n- A subject can be observed by the same observer through two paths (diamond pattern)\n\nThe code compiles successfully with C++20 and has no external dependencies. The implementation uses:\n- `std::vector<std::weak_ptr<Observer>>` for observer storage to avoid circular references\n- Proper mutex locking for thread safety\n- Atomic variables for thread-safe computation tracking\n- Simple vector-based caching to avoid complex hash map issues\n\nThe build was verified to work correctly with `make` in the build directory, and simple tests confirm all components function as expected.",
